; Latin > Vulgar Latin: the loss of h.
; Vulgar Latin > Western Romance: stress, the vowel merger, the first
; lenition. Stress comes after Vulgar Latin, since cells re-formed at
; Western Romance are joined from Vulgar Latin forms and need stressing.

categories
B = &+
Vs = a e i o u
Vl = ā ē ī ō ū ae au oe
Ss = á é í ó ú
Sl = ā́ ḗ ī́ ṓ ū́ áe áu óe
V = Vs Vl
S = Ss Sl
Stop = p b t d k g kʷ gʷ
L = l r
C = Stop f s h m n l r j w z β ʎ ɲ ts dz
; ° marks a clitic; it keeps stress off the word
U = °
end

h / / _
; the weak perfect: -āvit > -aut, stressed (Spanish cantó)
ā w i t / áu t / _ #
; and -īvit > -ió (Spanish murió)
ī w i t / j ṓ t / _ #

report

; Forms are joined without boundaries inside them (family.yaml). Those at
; the edges of bound items keep stems and affixes from being stressed as
; words.

; --- Stress ---
; monosyllables
V / S / # C* _ C* #
; a heavy penult: long, or closed (not before a stop and liquid)
Vl / Sl / _ C* V C* #
Vs / Ss / _ C C C* V C* # // _ Stop L V C* #
; otherwise the antepenult, if there is one
V / S / _ C* Vs (C) V C* # / _ C* Vs Stop L V C* #
; otherwise the penult
V / S / _ C* V C* # // S C* _

; clitics stay unstressed
° / / _

; --- Vowels ---
; quem > quien: final m of a stressed monosyllable
m / n / # C* S _ #
m / / [V S] _ #
; final n of neuters in -men
n / / V _ #
[e i] / j / _ [V S] // r _ á
[ā́ á ḗ é ī́ í ṓ ó ū́ ú áe óe áu] / [á á é ɛ́ í é ó ɔ́ ú ó ɛ́ é áu]
[ā ē ī ō ū ae oe i u] / [a e i o u e e e o]

categories
Vw = a e i o u au
Sw = á é ɛ́ í ó ɔ́ ú áu
W = Vw Sw
end

; --- Consonants ---
; prothesis before s and a stop
/ e / # _ s [p t k]
s / z / W _ W
; palatalisation and yod
; between vowels, voiced (dezir, plaisir); tj stays voiceless (cabeça)
k / dz / W _ [e i é í ɛ́ j]
k / ts / _ [e i é í ɛ́ j]
g / j / _ [e i é í ɛ́]
l j / ʎ / _
n j / ɲ / _
k t / j t / _
t j / ts / _
ts j / ts / _
; Latin d: voiced stops, unlike t, are already weak (pede > pie, pié)
d / ð / W _ [W r]
w / β / _
b / β / [W r l] _ [W r l]
; The voicing of p, t, k is not shared: Old French has syncope before it
; (comite > conte, doit), Spanish after it (conde).

; post-tonic vowel before l in a proparoxytone (oculus, populus)
o / / Sw C _ l W C* #
; -kl-, -gl-
[k g] l / ʎ / W _
